DIAGNOSIS confirmed at AS1 vantage point.

Findings (locally tested on AS1):
1. `dig @4.2.2.1 acm.org` returns A 198.82.0.99 with the `aa` flag (authoritative-style answer, TTL 0). The answer is not the result of a recursive lookup — it is hardcoded.
2. Process inspection: the listener on 4.2.2.1:53 is a dnsmasq instance launched with `--local=/acm.org/ --address=/acm.org/198.82.0.99`. It is the *only* process bound to 4.2.2.1:53 in my namespace; there is no real recursive resolver behind it.
