4. Cross-check: a separate authoritative dnsmasq on AS2 (154.54.1.1) answers acm.org → 198.82.0.1, which matches the reachable host. The 198.82.0.99 mapping on my resolver is therefore wrong, not a deliberate sinkhole of a live service.

ROOT CAUSE: AS1's recursive resolver is misconfigured — it serves a static, stale A record (198.82.0.99) for acm.org instead of recursing. Correct value is 198.82.0.1.

PROPOSED FIX (requires admin approval on my side): replace the static `--address=/acm.org/198.82.0.99` override with either (a) no override (allow real recursion) or (b) `--address=/acm.org/198.82.0.1` until the upstream zone is fixed. This affects DNS service for all my customers and touches the resolver configuration, so per policy I am NOT applying it unilaterally.

